      "costUsd": 0.010353000000000001,
      "pronunciationText": "Here's the cosine curve, with x in radians. Let's give it a meaning. It's the swell at a marker buoy off a surf beach: x is the time in seconds, which this model also uses as the angle in radians, one radian per second, and y is the buoy's height in metres above calm water. Now change the equation to y equals two cos of x minus pi over three, plus one. That's a second buoy further along the beach, on a day with bigger swell and a higher tide. The curve gets taller, lifts up and slides. But look at the peak. The bracket says minus pi over three, yet the peak has moved right, to pi over three. Each part of the equation does one job. Let's take them one at a time."
    },
