      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 100,
      "outputTokens": 735,
      "costUsd": 0.006665,
      "pronunciationText": "Now add one, outside the bracket. That's the tide coming in: every height goes up by one, so the whole curve slides up one unit. Its middle line, the midline, moves from the x-axis to y equals one. The shape doesn't change, so the amplitude is still two. The highest value is the midline plus the amplitude, three, and the lowest is the midline minus the amplitude, minus one. So the range is from minus one to three."
