      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 128,
      "outputTokens": 944,
      "costUsd": 0.00856,
      "pronunciationText": "Now the surprising one, inside the bracket. The second buoy is further along the beach, so each wave reaches it a little later. Its height now is what the first buoy's height was pi over three seconds ago. That's cos of x minus pi over three. The first buoy peaked where the inside was zero. Now the inside is zero when x equals pi over three. Everything happens pi over three later, so the graph slides right by pi over three. That's a horizontal translation. The minus sign means later, a slide to the right. A plus sign would mean earlier, a slide to the left."
    },
