      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 131,
      "outputTokens": 1033,
      "costUsd": 0.0093625,
      "pronunciationText": "What about a number multiplying x? A choppy swell brings waves twice as often. In y equals cos two x, the inside runs twice as fast as x. One full cycle needs the inside to go from zero to two pi, and that's finished when x reaches pi. So the period, the time for one cycle, halves to pi, about three seconds. The graph is squashed towards the y-axis, a horizontal dilation by a factor of one half. For sine and cosine with positive a, the period is two pi divided by ay. A half inside would double the period to four pi, a long, slow groundswell."
    },
