      "inputTokens": 131,
      "outputTokens": 1038,
      "costUsd": 0.0094075,
      "pronunciationText": "When there's a number multiplying x and a number added, take the number out first. Here's y equals sine of two x plus pi. It's tempting to say it slides left by pi. But the inside is zero when two x plus pi is zero, which is at x equals minus pi over two. Factor out the two, and you get sine of two, bracket x plus pi over two. So, squash by a factor of a half, then slide left by pi over two. Sliding left by pi would land right back on sine two x, which is wrong: the true curve is upside down compared with it."
    },
